<code>assert (\result == true) => this.size() == \old(this.size()) + 1;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert (\result => this.size() == \old(this.size()) + 1) && (!\result => this.size() == \old(this.size()));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert (\old(this.size()) + 1 == this.size()) => \result;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert (\old(this.size()) + 1 == this.size()) => this.add(word);</code>

However, the correct interpretation of the comment and the logic in the code should lead us to:

<code>assert !\old(this.contains(word)) => \old(this.size()) + 1 == this.size();</code>

This ensures that the size of the Trie increases by 1 only if the word was not already present in the Trie.
